-- title:
--   Diamond operators on the function field of X_H(q²M'), q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$. Put $N = q^2M'$ and let $H = \operatorname{ker}\big((\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\big)$ be the subgroup [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), and $\Gamma_H(N)$ the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the map $\Gamma_0(N) \to (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ sending $\gamma$ to its lower-right entry. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L((\mathsf{q}))/L$ assumed equal to the base change [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $\mathsf{q}$-expansion function field of $X_H(N)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. the subfield of $L((\mathsf{q}))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of that rational field. Then there is a monoid homomorphism $\rho \colon \Gamma_0(N) \to (K \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[L]} K)$ with four properties. (i) For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$, every weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, all modular forms $f, g, f_1, g_1$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H(N)$ (viewed inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$), all integral power series $p_f, p_g, p_{f_1}, p_{g_1}$ that are integral $\mathsf{q}$-expansions (at width $1$) of $f, g, f_1, g_1$ respectively, and every $c \in \mathbb{C}^\times$ with $f_1 = c\,(f \mid_k \gamma)$ and $g_1 = c\,(g \mid_k \gamma)$ as functions on the upper half-plane, if the Laurent series over $L$ attached to $p_g$ and to $p_{g_1}$ are nonzero, then every $x \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is $p_f/p_g$ (coefficients pushed into $L$) satisfies that $\rho(\gamma)x$ has underlying Laurent series $p_{f_1}/p_{g_1}$. (ii) Each $\rho(\gamma)$ fixes pointwise every element of $K$ lying in the base change to $L$ of the full modular function field of level $N$, the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $\mathsf{q}$-expansions of $j(d\tau)$ for $d \mid N$. (iii) Conversely every $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ fixing that subfield pointwise equals $\rho(\gamma)$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$. (iv) $\rho(\gamma) = 1$ if and only if the lower-right entry of $\gamma$, as a unit mod $N$, lies in $H \sqcup$-join with the subgroup generated by $-1$.
--
--   This is the description of the diamond operators as the group of $L$-automorphisms of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ over the floor $X_0(q^2M')$, with the kernel identified as the classes of determinant-type units congruent to $\pm 1$ modulo $q$; it is the $q = 2$ instance of the statement, the conclusion being the same as for larger $q$. It feeds the construction of elements of the chart algebra at infinity with prescribed leading coefficients used on the Igusa-tower leg of the argument.
